      "side": 0,
      "message": "`rsrc.permissions().check(ChangePermission.SUBMIT);` This is the line in the `apply` method. Since it calls permissions on `rsrc` (instead of specifying the user) it will check the permission of the user who called the REST API method (not the onBehalfOf user, which at that point has not been parsed/looked up yet)\n\n\u003e The Submit check in the apply condition is for the onbehalf of user, but it should be done for the real user.\n\nSo I think this is incorrect. But since this is causing some confusion, I am also open to re-writing it in a way which is clearer",
